.TH SWAPON 8 "August 2026" ReBSD
.SH NAME
swapon \- enable a Linux swap partition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swapon
.I special
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swapon
makes the block device named by
.I special
available to the machine-independent VM pager.
The caller must be the super-user.
.PP
Devices enabled at run time must contain a valid Linux swap version 1
header with the
.B SWAPSPACE2
signature.  The header page is reserved, the recorded last-page boundary is
honoured, and pages listed as bad in the header are excluded from allocation.
.PP
RAM-backed raw swap configured for an embedded platform at kernel build time
continues to use that platform's existing boot-time configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
swapon /dev/wd0b
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swapon (2),
.BR free (1),
.BR pstat (8)
.SH BUGS
ReBSD currently supports one active swap device.  There is no
.B swapoff
operation; reboot before removing or reformatting an active swap device.
